        <p class="pex">Claim. This continues #10393 and #10529 with the same definitions. A convex set C ∋ e of a finite Weyl group is {w : N(w) ⊆ U}, with δC(t) the share of C whose inversion set contains t, and b(C) = maxt min(δ, 1−δ). Gaetz–Gao (arXiv:2005.097…</p>
        
